From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommbe: sbe1v1k: enable the IPQ9574 PCS clock providers

设备取证（2026-11-18，v3 PHY 修复后的生产镜像）：MDIO 扫描已全绿
（0x10-0x13、0x1c 全部绑定），WAN eth1 载波 1 Gbps 但 RX 恒为 0、
DHCP discover 无人应答，dmesg 每 ~0.37 s 刷一条：

  nss_cc_port5_tx_clk_src: can't find a configuration for rate ...

栈是 qca_hppe_mac_sw_sync_task → ssdk_port_speed_clock_set →
ssdk_uniphy_clock_rate_set → clk_rcg2_fm_determine_rate →
__clk_rcg2_select_conf。

根因在时钟树：nsscc 的 port5 RX/TX 时钟源表以 UNIPHY0/1 的
NSS RX/TX 时钟为父（nss_cc_parent_data_0 的 DT 索引 4..9），而这些
父时钟由 mainline PCS 驱动（pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c，ipq_pcs_clk_register()
注册 "%s::rx_clk"/"%s::tx_clk"）提供。板级 DTS 把 pcs0/pcs1/pcs2 全部
disabled，内核配置也没打开 CONFIG_PCS_QCOM_IPQ9574，于是
clk_hw_get_parent_by_index() 对每个候选 conf 都返回 NULL，
__clk_rcg2_select_conf() 一个可用配置都选不出来 → WARN，port5 的
时钟永远设不上。CCF 的父时钟是懒解析、失败不缓存
（clk_core_fill_parent_index），所以只要提供者注册起来即可，
无需关心它与 nsscc 的 probe 先后。

共存性与 qca-ssdk 无冲突：qca-ssdk 通过自己 DT 节点 "ess-uniphy" 的
裸 ioremap 访问同一地址段（ioremap 不占 IORESOURCE_MEM region），
PCS 驱动 probe 只 ioremap 自己那三个 64 KiB 窗口、打开 sys/ahb 时钟、
注册时钟提供者，不写 UNIPHY 寄存器；写寄存器的 ops 只有 phylink
消费者才会调用，而本内核的 dp 端口都没有 pcs-handle。PCS 时钟在
没有消费者时 recalc_rate 固定返回 125 MHz（SGMII 1G），正是 port5
需要的父时钟速率。

v3（2026-11-18，真机取证后回退）：v2 曾在 pcs0/1/2 覆盖里
/delete-property/ resets;，想让 ssdk 成为 uniphy0/1/2_xpcs_rst 的
唯一持有者、消掉 3 条 __reset_control_get_internal WARN。刷机后取证：
镜像确实启动到了用户态（p27 尾部 overlay 里有完整的 sbe-boot-trace、
nss-load "tier wired loaded"、uci-defaults 已执行），但 10G 管理口
（eth0）没有任何流量，设备不可达。可见把 XPCS resets 交给 ssdk 独占
会改变端口初始化行为。因此 resets 保留在 DTS 里，接受那 3 条 WARN
作为已知噪声：PCS 驱动只消费时钟，从不 assert 该句柄（本内核没有带
pcs-handle 的 dp 端口），功能上无影响。

diff -ruN a/target/linux/qualcommbe/config-6.12 b/target/linux/qualcommbe/config-6.12
--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/config-6.12	2026-11-18 12:24:38.569286794 +0000
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/config-6.12	2026-11-18 12:24:38.579968892 +0000
@@ -328,7 +328,7 @@
 CONFIG_PCI_DOMAINS=y
 CONFIG_PCI_DOMAINS_GENERIC=y
 CONFIG_PCI_MSI=y
-# CONFIG_PCS_QCOM_IPQ9574 is not set
+CONFIG_PCS_QCOM_IPQ9574=y
 CONFIG_PER_VMA_LOCK=y
 CONFIG_PGTABLE_LEVELS=3
 CONFIG_PHYLIB=y
diff -ruN a/target/linux/qualcommbe/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574-sbe1v1k.dts b/target/linux/qualcommbe/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574-sbe1v1k.dts
--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574-sbe1v1k.dts	2026-11-18 12:24:38.581883480 +0000
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574-sbe1v1k.dts	2026-11-18 12:24:38.582856072 +0000
@@ -523,22 +523,38 @@
 };

 /*
- * UNIPHY register block consumed by qca-ssdk (ssdk_dt_parse_uniphy(), and
- * the uniphy clock provider in ssdk_clk.c).  It covers the three 64 KiB
- * mainline ethernet-pcs windows, so disable those nodes: their driver is not
- * built into this kernel (CONFIG_PCS_QCOM_IPQ9574 is not set), and enabling
- * it later would fight qca-ssdk for the same registers.
+ * The mainline PCS driver registers the per-UNIPHY RX/TX clocks that NSSCC
+ * consumes as parents of the port clock-source dividers (nsscc "clocks"
+ * indices 4..9).  Without a provider those parents never resolve and every
+ * rate request on nss_cc_port5_*_clk_src hits the
+ * "can't find a configuration for rate" WARN in __clk_rcg2_select_conf, so
+ * the SGMII/2.5G WAN port can never be clocked and eth1 stays RX=0.
+ *
+ * Coexistence with qca-ssdk is safe: qca-ssdk reaches the UNIPHY registers
+ * through a bare ioremap of its own "ess-uniphy" node and parses the block
+ * itself; the PCS driver only maps its own 64 KiB windows and does not
+ * touch the hardware until a phylink consumer calls its ops, and none
+ * exists in this kernel (no pcs-handle on any dp port).
+ *
+ * The XPCS reset lines stay in place.  qca-ssdk requests the same three
+ * resets exclusively through its own gcc reset ids (ssdk_clk.c), so the PCS
+ * driver's devm_reset_control_get_optional() trips the shared/exclusive WARN
+ * in the reset core and fails with -EBUSY on every boot.  That is harmless:
+ * the driver never asserts the handle (no dp port carries a pcs-handle), it
+ * only needs its clocks.  Deleting the property was tried on 2026-11-18: the
+ * image still booted into userspace, but the 10G dp port never came up, so
+ * qca-ssdk must not be the only owner of the XPCS resets.
  */
 &pcs0 {
-	status = "disabled";
+	status = "okay";
 };

 &pcs1 {
-	status = "disabled";
+	status = "okay";
 };

 &pcs2 {
-	status = "disabled";
+	status = "okay";
 };

 &soc {
